---
# Clang-tidy configuration for the C sources in this repository.
#
# Scope: firmware core (src/core, src/stage, src/source, include/) and the
# host harness (host/). The platform layer (src/platform/zmk) is analyzed by
# the same configuration through the firmware compile database (see
# docs/quality.md, issue #76).
#
# The check set favors correctness (bugprone, clang-analyzer, misc,
# portability) over style; style is enforced by clang-format instead.
# Cognitive complexity complements the lizard cyclomatic gate; the threshold
# is a ratchet set above the worst host-compiled firmware function. Service-
# layer functions (src/service, src/platform) are not in the host compile
# database, and their cognitive values are inflated by Zephyr's logging-macro
# expansion (see docs/quality.md).
#
# Excluded:
# - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: pure noise for this codebase
#   (parameters are documented in headers).
# - clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.*: the recommended C11 Annex K
#   bounded alternatives (sscanf_s & co.) do not exist on the Zephyr/newlib
#   target, and the only affected code parses trusted local input read into
#   bounded buffers by fgets().
# - clang-analyzer-optin.*: opt-in analyzers are enabled explicitly, not
#   pulled in by the clang-analyzer-* wildcard. Newer tool versions extend
#   the opt-in set (the 22 series flags e.g. optin.performance.Padding on
#   struct zpt_route_override), which would fail a clean tree on a tool
#   bump; enable a specific opt-in analyzer deliberately if wanted.
# - misc-include-cleaner: churn-only for a codebase with stable includes.
# - misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes: C++-only.
# - performance-enum-size: enums are used as typed constants; resizing them
#   would change ABI without benefit.
# - portability-avoid-pragma-once: the repository's standard header guard is
#   #pragma once (every include/ and host/ header uses it); converting to
#   include guards is churn with no correctness benefit. Recent clang-tidy
#   versions (22+) flag pragma once in included headers aggressively, which
#   would fail a clean tree depending on the toolchain version in use.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.*,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.*,
  misc-*,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  performance-*,
  -performance-enum-size,
  portability-*,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once,
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
CheckOptions:
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.Threshold: '25'
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.DescribeBasicIncrements: 'true'
